== the cafe ==

-- 0. the application starts
ok 0.1 the page scan refused nothing
ok 0.2 the form scan refused nothing
ok 0.3 the shell options have no faults
ok 0.4 latte and latte.web agree where the client is served
ok 0.5 latte and latte.web agree where the socket is

-- 1. GET / is a document, not a fragment
ok 1.1 status
ok 1.2 content type
ok 1.3 the content security policy
ok 1.4 nosniff
ok 1.5 no framing
ok 1.6 referrer
ok 1.7 a session cookie was minted, 256 bits of it
ok 1.8 the cookie is HttpOnly
ok 1.9 the cookie is SameSite=Lax
ok 1.10 and NOT Secure, because this app serves plain http
ok 1.11 it is a document
ok 1.12 the client is loaded from latte's own path
ok 1.13 no inline script
ok 1.14 no inline style
ok 1.15 no on* handler attribute
ok 1.16 no circuit id in the page at all
ok 1.17 the page body is inside the root element

--- the document ---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>The Cafe</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css">
<script src="/_latte/latte.js" defer data-latte-boot="1" data-latte-ws="/_latte/ws" data-latte-root="latte-root"></script>
</head>
<body>
<div id="latte-root"><div class="page"><header><h1>The Cafe</h1><nav><a href="/">menu</a><a href="/order/4">order for table 4</a></nav></header><main><section class="menu"><h2>Menu</h2><ul id="drinks"><li class="drink"><button type="button" data-drink="espresso">espresso — 190p</button></li><li class="drink"><button type="button" data-drink="flat white">flat white — 320p</button></li><li class="drink"><button type="button" data-drink="cortado">cortado — 280p</button></li></ul><p id="picked">nothing picked yet</p></section></main></div></div>
</body>
</html>

--- end of the document ---

-- 2. the client script is served, and cached honestly
ok 2.1 the page points at the path the asset route claims
ok 2.2 status
ok 2.3 content type
ok 2.4 the bytes are the file's, all of them
ok 2.5 revalidate rather than cache blind
ok 2.6 it carries a strong entity tag
ok 2.7 nosniff reaches the script too, so the type has to be right
ok 2.8 a matching tag is 304
ok 2.9 and carries no body
ok 2.10 a stale tag gets the whole file
ok 2.11 all of it
ok 2.12 POST to a static asset is 405
ok 2.13 and says what it does answer
ok 2.14 the stylesheet is served by the same route
ok 2.15 as css

-- 3. the order form, with JavaScript switched off
ok 3.1 status
ok 3.2 the token's MAC is a SHA-256 digest
ok 3.3 the route parameter reached the page

--- /order/4, with the token masked ---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>The Cafe</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css">
<script src="/_latte/latte.js" defer data-latte-boot="1" data-latte-ws="/_latte/ws" data-latte-root="latte-root"></script>
</head>
<body>
<div id="latte-root"><div class="page"><header><h1>The Cafe</h1><nav><a href="/">menu</a><a href="/order/4">order for table 4</a></nav></header><main><section class="order"><h2>Order for table 4</h2><form method="post" action="/order/4"><input type="hidden" name="__latte_token" value="TOKEN"><label>name <input name="name" id="name" value=""></label><label>cups <input name="cups" id="cups" value="0"></label><label>decaf <input type="checkbox" name="decaf" id="decaf"></label><button type="submit" id="place">place the order</button></form><ul id="problems"></ul><p id="placed">no order placed</p></section></main></div></div>
</body>
</html>

--- end ---
ok 3.4 a good POST is accepted
ok 3.5 and the order is placed
ok 3.6 a bad POST is still a page
ok 3.7 the length rule is reported by name
ok 3.8 the range rule is reported by name
ok 3.9 and the boxes give back what was typed
ok 3.10 nothing was placed
ok 3.11 a POST with no token is refused
ok 3.12 a forged token is refused
ok 3.13 the second visitor got a different session
ok 3.14 another session's token is refused
ok 3.15 a table that is not a number is refused
ok 3.16 a path no @page claims falls through to espresso

-- 4. a click, over a circuit
ok 4.1 the circuit opened
ok 4.2 one frame is queued before any message
ok 4.3 and it is the hello, naming the id the SERVER minted
ok 4.4 attach answers exactly one batch
ok 4.5 it is batch 1
ok 4.6 the whole menu is in it
ok 4.7 including the page's own text
ok 4.8 three drinks bound three click handlers
   the handler ids the batch carried: 3, 5, 7
ok 4.9 a click answers one batch
ok 4.10 it is batch 2
ok 4.11 the page says what was picked
ok 4.12 and an untouched row is not on the wire
ok 4.13 a click on a stale-looking slot still lands
ok 4.14 on the row it belongs to
ok 4.15 one circuit is held
ok 4.16 and the set recorded no faults

69 checks, 0 bad
